      "transcriber_notes": [
        "56 data rows (years 1865-1920) counted on the page; 56 transcribed, plus the sub-heading row 'HANKOW GAUGE ESTABLISHED :—' (printed between 1867 and 1868) and the 'Bund level 46 6' line printed below the closing rule under the Highest River Feet/Inches columns.",
        "Title says 'from 1865 to 1919' but the table runs to 1920; kept as printed.",
        "Feet figures prefixed '—' are printed with a minus/dash meaning 'Below Zero' (footnote); '†' prefix = 'About Bund level' (footnote); both kept as printed in the cell.",
        "Dates: month and day printed with dot leaders; written as 'Month day' with leaders dropped.",
        "1869 Lowest River Feet: printed '10' with the '1' set slightly lower and smaller than the '0' (possibly a displaced type); transcribed as printed, '10'.",
        "1877 Highest River Feet printed '24' (checked at full resolution); kept as printed although far below neighbouring years.",
        "1910 Highest River Feet '49' has no † although other years at 46-50 do; as printed.",
        "Year labels 1889 ('1›89'), 1904 ('!904') and 1910 ('!910') have damaged digits in the scan; the rest of each numeral is clear and the years run in unbroken sequence.",
        "No totals printed."
      ],
